        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0387" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1041"/>

                <head>No. 493.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Schuyler to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 9, 1875</date>.
                        (Received March 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 83.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my dispatch No. 82, on the subject of
                    the Brussels congress, I spoke of a dispatch which had recently been received
                    from Lord Derby.</p>
                <p>I have now the honor to inclose to you, cut from the London Daily Telegraph, and
                    marked 1, a printed copy of this dispatch, which bears date the 20th of
                    January.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EUGENE SCHUYLER.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d194-a1.xml" xpointer="d194-a1"/>
            </div>
